atlas institutional-worlds

architecture institutional-worlds
  canonical_name InstitutionalWorlds
  owns WorldPolicy
  consumes EffectIntent
  consumes InformationPolicy
  consumes DelegationEnvelope
  publishes WorldPolicy
  publishes EffectAdmission
  family institutional
  domain Institution / Execution world
  layer execution
  semantic_question In which world does this estate execute, and what happens to an effect intent raised inside it?
  purpose Give a prospect, a demo, a replay and a live client genuinely different execution semantics, so demonstration state and client state can never be confused for one another.
  maturity implemented
  node_types World
  node_types EffectPolicy
  node_types DemoInstitution
  node_types ClientInstitution
  edge_types executes_in
  edge_types converts_to
  invariant every institution declares exactly one world
  invariant the worlds this contract declares and the worlds the Matrix can bind are the same set; a world that cannot be bound to a host is a world no institution can actually execute in
  invariant a DEMO world admits real public observation but never a live external effect against a third party
  invariant demo state is synthetic or replayed and is never merged into client state
  invariant conversion from DemoInstitution to ClientInstitution is an explicit transition that re-derives policies, effects and data closure rather than relabelling the institution
  invariant usage and financial projection are recorded in DEMO as proposal economics, never as revenue
  forbidden_inference a demo exercising a capability -> that capability being authorized live
  forbidden_inference demo data resembling client data -> demo data being usable as client data
  forbidden_inference conversion -> demo history becoming client history
  invariant an institution's world is registered once in the Matrix and applies to every host it serves; a per-host world would let one institution be DEMO on one address and LIVE on another
  invariant an institution that declares no world is LIVE; the failure directions are not symmetric, and an estate that forgets must be treated as real rather than silently sandboxed
  invariant a DEMO institution has no settlement facilitator regardless of what the environment configures; the world overrides configuration, or it is a label rather than a property of execution
  forbidden_inference a world named in this contract -> a world the Matrix can bind (they were four and four with three in common: DEMO was declared and unbindable, CANDIDATE bindable and undeclared)
  source_path engine/core/include/bf_matrix.h
  source_path engine/core/src/matrix.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  witness a capability quote served with a facilitator configured returns facilitator_configured true for a LIVE institution and false for a DEMO institution on the same running binary
  known_gap only settlement is gated by world today; other external effects -- outbound publication, foreign observation writes -- do not yet consult institution_world
  interacts institutional-root
  interacts delegation-model
  interacts institutional-relationship-types
  source_lineage Generation-10 product topology separation, 2026-08-26

world LIVE
  detail Real institution, real data, real effects subject to authority and admission.
world DEMO
  detail Prospect-facing. Real public observation allowed, synthetic or replayed institution state, sandboxed effects, proposal economics.
world SHADOW
  detail Candidate execution against real state with effects withheld, used to prove a realization before promotion.
world REPLAY
  detail Deterministic re-execution of recorded occurrences for proof and divergence detection.
world CANDIDATE
  detail A proposed execution not yet admitted to any of the above. Implemented in the
  detail Matrix world enum before this contract named it, which is how DEMO came to be
  detail declared here and absent there: two lists of four worlds, three of them shared.
